        <headline>SYSTEMS BLEED AND PRESSURISATION REVIEW</headline>
        <description>BACKGROUND: A REVIEW OF ACMS HAS FOUND RH BLEED DUCT PRESSURE REMAINS  LOW IN CLIMB (29 PSI). FURTHER ACTION REQUIRED

ACTION:

1). OBSERVING ALL SAFETY PRECAUTIONS, GAIN ACCESS TO THE AIRCRAFT.

2). USING PNEUMATIC TESTING KIT (P/N 1945-04-08) PERFORM A COMPLETE PNEUMATIC HEALTH CHECK OF THE #2 BLEED COMPONENTS IAW AMM 36-11-00.

* RECORD THE RESULTS ON THE ATTACHED RA851 FORM AND SUBMIT TO BLEEDREVIEW@RYANAIR.COM   
** RECORD THE SERIAL NUMBER OF THE TEST KIT USED ON THE RA851 FORM ALSO.   

3). INSPECT ALL SYSTEM SENSE LINES AND CONNECTIONS FOR ANY SIGNS OF DAMAGE, BLOCKAGE OR LEAKAGE. MAKE THE NECESSARY RECTIFICATIONS.    

4). CLOSELY INSPECT RH PRSOV FOR NOTCHY BEHAVIOUR, INABILITY TO REMAIN OPEN AND ACTUATOR BODY LEAKAGE. REPLACE IF NEEDED IAW AMM TASK 36-11-04/401.    

5). CHECK BLEED AIR REGULATOR FOR D/S PORT LEAKAGE OR RUPTURED REVERSE FLOW DIAPHRAGM.    

6). LEAK CHECK ALL HSR / HSV / PCCV / BAR SENSE LINES USING SUITABLE LEAK CHECK SPRAY.    

7). IF NFF REPLACE THE  #2 450 SENSOR IAW AMM 36-11-05/401.

8). RETURN AC TO SERVICE WITH ALL FINDINGS FROM THIS WO DOCUMENTED AND CLOSED EITHER THROUGH POSITIVE MAINTENANCE ACTION OR AN ACCEPTABLE DEFERRAL

**AIRCRAFT IS EQUIPPED WITH ACMS - NO BLEED SHEETS WILL BE REQUIRED.     
**PLEASE ENSURE THAT ALL ELECTRICAL (WHERE APPLICABLE) AND PNEUMATIC FITTINGS / COMPONENTS DISTURBED DURING ABOVE WORKS ARE RE-INSTATED TO CORRECT CONFIGURATION AFTER WORKS.</description>
